{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe model-upgrade task `beaten-natural-grouse` moves the production compose defaults (`infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:97-99`) and the Bedrock CloudWatch alarm dimensions (`infra/terraform/monitoring_eb6e.tf:80-135`) to `us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5`, `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5` and `us.anthropic.claude-haiku-5-5`. The unit test `tests/unit/test_reviewbot_bedrock_cutover.py` proves the alarms name the same ids the bot invokes, but it cannot prove that Bedrock publishes metrics under exactly those `ModelId` strings. The alarms use `treat_missing_data = \"notBreaching\"` (`monitoring_eb6e.tf:42`), so a dimension that matches no published series would never page, silently.\n\n## Approach\n\nAfter the upgrade change has merged and the operator has applied the terraform and redeployed the production server, run the read-only `aws cloudwatch list-metrics --namespace AWS/Bedrock --metric-name Invocations --profile frontier --region us-east-1` and compare each listed `ModelId` with the three alarm dimensions character for character. If a 5.5 id is missing from the published series, or spelled differently, file a bug linked `discovered_from` this task with the listed series and the alarm values. Reading the published series is the only check that observes what CloudWatch actually keys on; production stays read-only (applying terraform and redeploying are operator steps, not part of this task).\n\n## Scope\n\nNone: this verification changes no repository file. Evidence lives in a comment on this ticket.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The `aws cloudwatch list-metrics` output, its PST timestamp, and the per-id match result for the three 5.5 `ModelId` dimensions are recorded in a ticket comment."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794260706657989001,"uuid":"ee92bfa8-9ca4-4c7d-9b35-4af87a981537"}